# WHAT GIT IGNORES, AND WHY
# Nir does not read code, so every rule here says what it is protecting.
# Rule of thumb for this project: we back up TRUTH, not artifacts
# (bible/part-12.md 12.2.4). Anything a machine can rebuild stays out of git.

# --- SECRETS. Never, ever committed (bible/part-07.md 7.4.2). ---
# Real API keys and passwords live in .env files on the home machines only.
# The .env.example file IS committed, because it holds only dummy values and
# documents what each secret is for.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- PYTHON WORKING FILES. Rebuilt by "uv sync" in seconds. ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- NODE WORKING FILES. Rebuilt by "npm install". ---
node_modules/

# --- BUILD OUTPUTS. Reproducible from the database, so not worth storing. ---
# The exports/ folder holds the finished website folders that Nir drags to the
# server. They are large, they are regenerated every week, and they must never
# be edited by hand (bible/part-00.md LAW 12). We keep the folder itself and
# the record of which version is currently live.
exports/*
!exports/.gitkeep
!exports/live-manifest.json
site/dist/

# --- THE FROZEN SOURCE CACHE. Large, and backed up by rsync instead. ---
# Raw article text and video transcripts are kept on disk as permanent
# evidence (bible/part-06.md 6.2.4) and copied to the laptop weekly. They are
# far too big for git.
pipeline/raw/
pipeline/scratch/

# --- GENERATED IMAGES. Re-renderable from the same prompt and seed. ---
comfy/output/

# --- DESKTOP AND EDITOR JUNK. Nobody needs these in a five-year archive. ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*~
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- THE HOMEMADE CERTIFICATE for showing the site to the headset. ---
# It contains a private key, and it is specific to this one computer, so it
# has no business in a shared repository (bible/part-07.md 7.4).
ops/local-certificate/

# --- BATCHES IN FLIGHT. Receipts for work paid for and not yet collected. ---
# Working files, not truth: the truth is the ledger and content/. They are
# machine-local because a batch belongs to the machine that submitted it.
pipeline/batches/
